From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:26:23 +0530
Subject: Skip the libstdc++ load under emscripten

Startup asks the interpreter to load libstdc++ so its symbols are available for
lookup. On wasm the standard library is libc++, statically linked into the
hosting module -- 5000-odd std:: symbols are already in xcpp.wasm -- so there is
nothing to load and no file of that name anywhere in the toolchain.

It is not a harmless no-op either. The name resolves to something fetchable that
is not wasm, so the loader reports "need to see wasm magic number" and leaves a
failed entry behind, which is noise directly above the far more interesting
errors in the console.

Natively the call is redundant too, since the process already has libstdc++
through the compiler default and the dlopen only bumps a refcount -- so this
guards the one platform where it does harm rather than removing it outright.

(cherry picked from commit 213d3aa0ca0b46f4b72629ddb8d48ec71010d19d)
---
 src/interop/interop_wrapper.cxx | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/interop/interop_wrapper.cxx b/src/interop/interop_wrapper.cxx
index c55bc05..88be5de 100644
--- a/src/interop/interop_wrapper.cxx
+++ b/src/interop/interop_wrapper.cxx
@@ -124,7 +124,13 @@ public:
     }
 
     Cpp::AddIncludePath(CPPINTEROP_INCLUDE_DIR);
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // Nothing to load under emscripten: the standard library there is libc++,
+    // statically linked into the hosting module. The name also resolves to
+    // something fetchable that is not wasm -- a 404 page -- so the loader
+    // reports "need to see wasm magic number" and leaves a failed entry behind.
     Cpp::LoadLibrary("libstdc++", /* lookup= */ true);
+#endif
 
     // load frequently used headers
     const char* code = "#include <algorithm>\n"
